16. Nvidia modules

The reddit post has the usual details, but there is more.
nvidia-utils package puts an entry in /usr/lib/modules-load.d/nvidia-utils.conf,
which makes systemd load the modules upon boot, which can be seen by:

$ journalctl -b --output=short-monotonic -u systemd-modules-load.service

Now, we can override this exact file by

$ touch /etc/modules-load.d/nvidia-utils.conf

This is because the /etc entries are preferred over the defaults in /usr/lib.
Blacklisting the nvidia modules in /etc/modprobe.d/blacklist-nvidia.conf
helps lighten the initcpio img. All this combined gives boost to boot times,
and saves battery.
For using the nvidia GPU, first load the modules using sudo /opt/hypr/nvidia.sh on

